As a sample-size control, subsampling C4 to $n{=}2{,}200$ (matching arXiv) yields $\Kempirical{=}1$ (1v2 $\auc = 0.601$, CI $[0.586, 0.616]$).
Reduced sample size widens confidence intervals and produces more conservative $\Kempirical$ estimates, arXiv's $\Kempirical{=}3$ at the same sample size therefore reflects genuine domain signal rather than a statistical artifact of smaller training sets.

